 result←object(State Pen)arg;style;color;size
 result←⍬
 ⍝ 'Pen' style [fgcolor] [size]
 ⍝ 'Pen' ¯1 hpen

 '∆WI LENGTH ERROR: Pen'##.Error~1 2 3∊⍨≢arg
 style←⊃arg
 'DOMAIN ERROR'##.Error(~##.IsInt style)∨0≠≡style
 '∆WI DRAW ERROR: Invalid pen style'##.Error~style∊¯1 0,⍳6
 :If 3=≢arg ⋄ :AndIf 1<3⊃arg ⋄ :andif style>2 ⋄ style←1 ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ If size>1 then force a solid or inside-solid line
 :Select style
 :Case ¯1
     '∆WI LENGTH ERROR: Pen'##.Error 2≠≢arg
     'DOMAIN ERROR'##.Error~##.IsInt 2⊃arg
     State._pen←arg ⍝ Store only 2⍴ in this case
 :Case 0
     State._pen←,style ⍝ Color & size completely ignored for transparent pens; store only 1⍴0
 :Else
     arg,←arg≢⍛↓1(2⊃State._color_)1 ⍝ Append defaults
     (color size)←1↓arg ⍝ Style already assigned, checked and possibly modified
     :If 0=≢color ⋄ color←2⊃State._color_ ⋄ :EndIf
     'DOMAIN ERROR'##.Error~##.IsInt color
     ⍝ Note that APL+Win produces an incorrectly-labelled error message here -- we'll duplicate the incorrect text in case they depend on it
     '∆WI LENGTH ERROR: Brush'##.Error~color≢⍛∊1 3
     '∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Brush'##.Error(3=≢color)∧∨/(color<0)∨color≥256
     '∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Brush'##.Error(1=≢color)∨∨/color≥256*3
     '∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Brush'##.Error(1=≢color)∨∨/(color<0)∧color≥¯100
     'DOMAIN ERROR'##.Error(~##.IsInt size)∨(1<≢⍴size)∨1≠≢size
     State._pen←style color(⊃size) ⍝ Remember this setting (3⍴)
 :EndSelect
